    "transcript": [
      {
        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "Welcome to Holiday Hour. This week, we're talking about walking holidays in the north of England. Many people think walking holidays are only for experts, but that isn't true. You can choose a route for beginners or for experienced walkers. The most popular route is the Lake Trail. It is about forty kilometres long, and most people finish it in four days. You stay in small hotels each night, and a van carries your bags, so you only carry water and a lunch. The best time to go is between May and September, when the days are long and the weather is usually dry. However, you should always take a rain jacket, because the weather can change quickly. Good boots are very important too. Don't buy new boots just before the trip, because they can hurt your feet. A group holiday costs about four hundred pounds, including hotels, dinners and the van. If you go alone, it's more expensive. Booking early is a good idea, because the popular weeks in July and August are often full. For more information, visit our website, where you can also see a short film about the Lake Trail."
      }
    ]
